{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# PredictGuard — Phase 1, Stage 5: Baseline and Stronger Models\n",
    "\n",
    "**Project**: Explainable Predictive Maintenance System  \n",
    "**Dataset**: Microsoft Azure Predictive Maintenance  \n",
    "**Author**: PredictGuard Contributors  \n",
    "**Stage**: 5 of 6 — Baseline and Stronger Models\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Objective\n",
    "\n",
    "Establish **strong baseline models** (Logistic Regression, Random Forest, XGBoost) trained on the Development set (80 machines) and evaluated on the held-out Final Test set (20 unseen machines).  \n",
    "All computational logic lives in `src/train.py`.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Evaluation Rationale: Why PR-AUC is the Primary Metric\n",
    "\n",
    "> In predictive maintenance with extreme class imbalance (~1.9% positive failure rate), **Accuracy is misleading**: a dummy model predicting all 0s achieves 98.1% accuracy but 0.0 recall. **PR-AUC (Precision-Recall AUC / Average Precision)** measures performance specifically on the rare failure class."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 0. Environment Setup & Imports"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import logging\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "import time\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import matplotlib\n",
    "\n",
    "# Ensure src/ is importable\n",
    "project_root = Path.cwd().parent\n",
    "if str(project_root) not in sys.path:\n",
    "    sys.path.insert(0, str(project_root))\n",
    "\n",
    "from src import train as tr\n",
    "\n",
    "logging.basicConfig(\n",
    "    level=logging.INFO,\n",
    "    format=\"%(asctime)s | %(levelname)-8s | %(name)s | %(message)s\",\n",
    "    datefmt=\"%H:%M:%S\",\n",
    "    handlers=[logging.StreamHandler(sys.stdout)],\n",
    ")\n",
    "logger = logging.getLogger(\"stage5_notebook\")\n",
    "logger.info(\"Stage 5 notebook started.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "PROCESSED_DIR = project_root / \"data\" / \"processed\"\n",
    "REPORTS_DIR = project_root / \"reports\"\n",
    "FIGURES_DIR = REPORTS_DIR / \"figures\"\n",
    "MODELS_DIR = project_root / \"models\"\n",
    "\n",
    "MODELS_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "REPORTS_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "FIGURES_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 1. Load Development & Final Test Parquets"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "dev_df = pd.read_parquet(PROCESSED_DIR / \"development.parquet\")\n",
    "test_df = pd.read_parquet(PROCESSED_DIR / \"test.parquet\")\n",
    "\n",
    "trainer = tr.ModelTrainer(random_seed=42)\n",
    "X_train, y_train, feature_names = trainer.prepare_data(dev_df)\n",
    "X_test, y_test, _ = trainer.prepare_data(test_df)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"X_train shape: {X_train.shape[0]:,} rows x {X_train.shape[1]} features (80 machines)\")\n",
    "print(f\"X_test shape:  {X_test.shape[0]:,} rows x {X_test.shape[1]} features (20 unseen machines)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 2. Train Model 1: Logistic Regression Baseline\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Why Scaling is Required:** Gradient-based optimization relies on input scale. `StandardScaler` is wrapped inside an `sklearn.pipeline.Pipeline`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "evaluator = tr.ModelEvaluator()\n",
    "saver = tr.ModelSaver()\n",
    "eval_results = {}\n",
    "\n",
    "lr_model = trainer.build_logistic_regression()\n",
    "t0 = time.time()\n",
    "lr_model.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
    "fit_time_lr = time.time() - t0\n",
    "\n",
    "lr_eval = evaluator.evaluate(\"Logistic Regression\", lr_model, X_test, y_test, fit_time_sec=fit_time_lr)\n",
    "eval_results[\"Logistic Regression\"] = lr_eval\n",
    "saver.save(lr_model, \"Logistic Regression\", lr_eval, X_train, y_train, MODELS_DIR)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 3. Train Model 2: Random Forest Classifier\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Why Scaling is NOT Required:** Decision trees split feature spaces non-parametrically; scaling does not alter decision boundaries."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "rf_model = trainer.build_random_forest(n_estimators=100)\n",
    "t0 = time.time()\n",
    "rf_model.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
    "fit_time_rf = time.time() - t0\n",
    "\n",
    "rf_eval = evaluator.evaluate(\"Random Forest\", rf_model, X_test, y_test, fit_time_sec=fit_time_rf)\n",
    "eval_results[\"Random Forest\"] = rf_eval\n",
    "saver.save(rf_model, \"Random Forest\", rf_eval, X_train, y_train, MODELS_DIR)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 4. Train Model 3: XGBoost Classifier\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Automated Imbalance Handling:** `scale_pos_weight` is set to $(N_{neg} / N_{pos}) \\approx 50.0$."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "xgb_model = trainer.build_xgboost(y_train, n_estimators=100)\n",
    "t0 = time.time()\n",
    "xgb_model.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
    "fit_time_xgb = time.time() - t0\n",
    "\n",
    "xgb_eval = evaluator.evaluate(\"XGBoost\", xgb_model, X_test, y_test, fit_time_sec=fit_time_xgb)\n",
    "eval_results[\"XGBoost\"] = xgb_eval\n",
    "saver.save(xgb_model, \"XGBoost\", xgb_eval, X_train, y_train, MODELS_DIR)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 5. Comparative Evaluation Summary"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "summary_df = pd.DataFrame([\n",
    "    {\n",
    "        \"Model\": m,\n",
    "        \"PR-AUC (Primary)\": res[\"pr_auc\"],\n",
    "        \"ROC-AUC\": res[\"roc_auc\"],\n",
    "        \"F1 Score\": res[\"f1_score\"],\n",
    "        \"Recall\": res[\"recall\"],\n",
    "        \"Precision\": res[\"precision\"],\n",
    "        \"Fit Time (s)\": res[\"fit_time_sec\"],\
    "    }\n",
    "    for m, res in eval_results.items()\n",
    "]).sort_values(\"PR-AUC (Primary)\", ascending=False).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "display(summary_df)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 6. Generate Model Evaluation Dashboard & Markdown Report"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "tr.plot_model_evaluation_dashboard(eval_results, y_test, FIGURES_DIR)\n",
    "stats = {\"test_machines\": test_df[\"machineID\"].nunique(), \"test_rows\": len(test_df)}\n",
    "tr.generate_training_report(eval_results, stats, REPORTS_DIR / \"model_training_report.md\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✅ Dashboard saved under reports/figures/model_evaluation_dashboard.png\")\n",
    "print(\"✅ Training report saved under reports/model_training_report.md\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 7. Stage 5 Summary & Next Steps\n",
    "\n",
    "| Deliverable | Status |\n",
